WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:19.604
"Hurry!" Zann urged the prisoners. "We need to get out of here fast!"

2
00:00:19.605 --> 00:00:26.680
He had opened all the cells, and now Boz and Teplo were helping him guide the released prisoners up the narrow stairway.

3
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:34.425
When everyone was at the top of the stairs and out of the Dousing spell's range, some of the stronger Reds began zapping the weaker Reds to safety.

4
00:00:34.426 --> 00:00:36.821
The king approached Zann.

5
00:00:36.822 --> 00:00:39.812
"Well done, young man," said the king.

6
00:00:39.813 --> 00:00:43.647
"You're a hero. I'm going to recommend that you . . ."

7
00:00:43.648 --> 00:00:48.205
Just then Zann heard a faint sound—it sounded like a heartbeat.

8
00:00:48.206 --> 00:00:51.004
He tried to ignore it, but it was impossible.

9
00:00:51.005 --> 00:00:56.788
It was as if the sound wouldn't let him think about anything else—it was forcing him to listen.

10
00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:03.162
"Your Majesty," said Zann, interrupting the king. "I'm sorry, but do you hear that sound?"

11
00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:07.659
The king gave Zann a funny look. "What sound are you talking about?"

12
00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.891
"It sounds like a heartbeat," said Zann.

13
00:01:10.892 --> 00:01:13.689
The king listened but didn't seem to hear it.

14
00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.124
Boz and Teplo hurried over to them.

15
00:01:16.125 --> 00:01:20.127
"Did you say you hear a heartbeat?" Teplo asked, looking anxious.

16
00:01:20.128 --> 00:01:25.049
"It's probably a Guiding spell! You said Fala is here in the palace, yes?"

17
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:31.176
Zann had no idea what Teplo was talking about. "What's a Guiding spell?" he asked.

18
00:01:31.177 --> 00:01:34.876
"It's a very old-fashioned spell," Teplo explained.

19
00:01:34.877 --> 00:01:42.871
"I taught Fala how to do it. Hardly anybody uses a Guiding spell these days—ever since message moths were discovered.

20
00:01:42.872 --> 00:01:49.330
But you never know when you might find yourself in a precarious situation without one of those moths."

21
00:01:49.331 --> 00:01:54.163
"You and your strange old tricks!" Boz laughed.

22
00:01:54.164 --> 00:01:57.216
"Focus on the sound, Zann," Teplo said.

23
00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:01.298
"Fala is directing it to you, so you're the only one who can hear it.

24
00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:05.620
The closer you get to Fala, the louder the sound will get."

25
00:02:05.621 --> 00:02:12.178
Zann focused on the heartbeat. He noticed that he could hear it slightly better if he turned toward the long hallway.

26
00:02:12.179 --> 00:02:16.286
He took a step in that direction and the sound became much more distinct.

27
00:02:16.287 --> 00:02:21.008
"I think we're supposed to go this way," said Zann, pointing down the hallway.

28
00:02:21.009 --> 00:02:24.842
"That leads to the ballroom," said the king.

29
00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:27.502
"To the ballroom!" Teplo commanded.

30
00:02:27.503 --> 00:02:31.560
Zann headed along the hallway, followed by all the freed Reds.

31
00:02:31.561 --> 00:02:36.381
With each step he took, he could hear the sound become louder and clearer.

32
00:02:36.382 --> 00:02:39.977
Soon they rounded a corner and arrived in the ballroom.

33
00:02:39.978 --> 00:02:45.266
Fala was there, along with Perda, Gliss, Darb, and all the rebels.

34
00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:48.478
As soon as Zann saw Fala, the sound stopped.

35
00:02:48.479 --> 00:02:52.200
The rebels gasped when they saw the freed Reds come into the room.

36
00:02:52.201 --> 00:02:57.113
"Mom! Dad!" Gliss cried, flinging herself into her parents' arms.

37
00:02:57.114 --> 00:03:00.986
"Gliss! You're safe!" Her mother hugged her tightly.

38
00:03:00.987 --> 00:03:06.261
"We were terribly worried about you," her father added. "And so was your uncle Gar."

39
00:03:06.262 --> 00:03:11.245
"I'm glad you're okay, Gliss," said Uncle Gar, who had just walked over.

40
00:03:11.246 --> 00:03:15.454
Meanwhile Perda and Darb rushed over to Zann, along with Zing.

41
00:03:15.455 --> 00:03:19.629
"You did it! You found the dungeon!" Perda exclaimed.

42
00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:25.054
Darb grinned and clapped Zann on the back while Zing flew in circles overhead, whistling.

43
00:03:25.055 --> 00:03:28.787
Zann was happy to see his friends, but he also felt nervous.

44
00:03:28.788 --> 00:03:31.225
Morb could show up at any moment.

45
00:03:31.226 --> 00:03:33.856
Nearby Fala was speaking with the king.

46
00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:38.659
"Your Majesty, Morb left the palace a short time ago," Fala told him.

47
00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:43.047
"But I'm not sure why, and I don't know when he'll return."

48
00:03:43.048 --> 00:03:48.303
The king nodded. Still weakened from the leech treatments, he spoke quietly to the crowd.

49
00:03:48.304 --> 00:03:56.073
"Citizens of Magica, I hereby declare Morb to be an enemy of our world," said the king.

50
00:03:56.074 --> 00:04:01.361
"Not since the Dark Times has Magica faced such a serious threat.

51
00:04:01.362 --> 00:04:05.988
Morb is to be arrested immediately when he returns."

52
00:04:05.989 --> 00:04:12.133
"Your Majesty, that might not be as easy as it sounds," said Boz.

53
00:04:12.134 --> 00:04:16.418
"Morb has become quite powerful in the last few days."

54
00:04:16.419 --> 00:04:23.127
"Even with all the Reds, we still might not be able to apprehend him," Vig added.

55
00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:26.515
"Then what are we going to do?" asked the queen.

56
00:04:26.516 --> 00:04:30.616
"We need a plan to ambush Morb," someone said.

57
00:04:30.617 --> 00:04:33.665
Growing impatient, Zann looked for his friends.

58
00:04:33.666 --> 00:04:37.331
Darb and Perda had gone over to join Gliss and her parents.

59
00:04:37.332 --> 00:04:40.851
Zing was nearby, nosing at a beetle on the floor.

60
00:04:40.852 --> 00:04:47.402
The far end of the ballroom opened out to the courtyard where Zann had seen Morb's magic-sucking machine.

61
00:04:47.403 --> 00:04:53.339
Zann wandered over, and he could see the machine crouched out there like a dark, terrible monster.

62
00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.124
Something new had been added to it since Zann had seen it yesterday.

63
00:04:57.125 --> 00:05:01.048
Perched at the very top was a strange-looking object.

64
00:05:01.049 --> 00:05:04.295
"What is that?" he murmured to himself.

65
00:05:04.296 --> 00:05:10.744
Zann stepped outside for a better look. When he got closer, he could see the new item more clearly.

66
00:05:10.745 --> 00:05:14.791
It was the jawbone from some kind of animal, perhaps a dragon.

67
00:05:14.792 --> 00:05:18.150
It was lined with large, razor-sharp teeth.

68
00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:25.061
Zann stood in front of the machine, staring at the pythons writhing in a tube filled with silvery liquid.

69
00:05:25.062 --> 00:05:28.161
Below that was a basin of dark water.

70
00:05:28.162 --> 00:05:34.851
Floating in the water was a multicolored, spongelike creature. Zann leaned in for a closer look.

71
00:05:34.852 --> 00:05:40.439
He'd never seen anything like it. Suddenly he heard a soft thump.

72
00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.895
Zann looked up to see that one of the pythons was looking right at him.

73
00:05:44.896 --> 00:05:48.166
Startled, Zann leaped backward with a gasp.

74
00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:54.581
Walking around to the other side of the machine, Zann examined the complicated network of bones and wire.

75
00:05:54.582 --> 00:05:57.354
How had Morb ever built such a thing?

76
00:05:57.355 --> 00:06:01.067
Just then Zann heard footsteps entering the courtyard.

77
00:06:01.068 --> 00:06:05.142
He quickly ducked behind a large plant and held his breath.

78
00:06:05.143 --> 00:06:15.161
His heart pounding, Zann peeked between the leaves and saw Morb, flanked by several ugly trolls.
